PH={
"lean":["Sipped slowly, lean takes about 30 to 60 minutes to be felt: a syrupy warmth in the chest and a slowing of thoughts, often with a heavy-tongued, slightly drunk feel from the promethazine.","Over the next hour the body gets heavy and movements slow down; music and conversation seem to stretch out, which is the 'leaning' slouch the drink is named for.","The peak, around 1.5 to 2.5 hours, combines codeine's mild warm euphoria with promethazine's heavy, dreamy drowsiness; itching, dry mouth and restless legs are common.","A long, slow-motion plateau of several hours in which people drift between dozing and waking.","Effects fade over about 4 to 6 hours, though promethazine's grogginess lasts longer; sleep is heavy.","Constipation, dry mouth, a thick head, and sometimes urinary trouble.","Next-day sluggishness is typical, and regular use brings dependence on codeine and weight gain from the sugary mixers."],
"kratom":["Swallowed kratom powder or tea usually begins within about 20 to 40 minutes, often first as a bitter taste, a slight warmth, and a mild lift in energy or calm depending on the amount and strain.","Over the next half hour, lower amounts feel coffee-like and talkative, while larger amounts bring a heavier, opioid-like body ease and sometimes nausea.","The peak, around 1 to 2 hours, is either a stimulating focus or a sedated calm with itching and pinpoint-ish pupils; too much brings 'the wobbles': dizziness, blurry eyes and vomiting.","A plateau of a few hours.","Effects fade over about 3 to 7 hours in total.","Constipation, dehydration, and a slightly flat mood.","Daily users can feel withdrawal (runny nose, aches, irritability, cravings) within a day of stopping."],
"7-hydroxymitragynine":["7-OH tablets or shots usually begin within about 15 to 30 minutes, much faster and stronger than plain kratom, with a clear opioid warmth.","The come-up is quick and smooth, with heaviness and itch.","The peak, around 1 hour, feels like a prescription opioid: euphoria, sedation, nodding, and slowed breathing at higher amounts.","A plateau of 1 to 3 hours.","Effects fade over about 3 to 5 hours, often leaving a craving to repeat.","Constipation, nausea, and low mood.","Dependence develops fast; withdrawal resembles prescription opioid withdrawal and the FDA moved to restrict 7-OH products in 2025."],
"desomorphine":["Injected street desomorphine hits within a minute or two with a strong, heroin-like rush of warmth.","There is almost no come-up; the rush is the come-up.","The peak is intense but short, with heavy sedation and euphoria.","The plateau lasts only about an hour.","Effects fade within 2 to 3 hours, which drives very frequent redosing.","Withdrawal and craving begin quickly; the toxic chemicals in homemade krokodil cause burning at the injection site.","With regular use, gangrene, bone and jaw damage, and severe infections appear within weeks or months."],
"etorphine":["In accidental human exposure, effects begin within seconds to minutes: sudden dizziness, heaviness and confusion.","There is no meaningful come-up before collapse can occur.","The 'peak' is profound sedation, pinpoint pupils and breathing that slows or stops.","Without treatment, it lasts for hours.","With naloxone or diprenorphine and medical care, recovery can still take hours, and sedation can return.","Exhaustion, nausea, possible brain injury from low oxygen.","Medical follow-up is needed."],
"dihydroetorphine":["Under the tongue, dihydroetorphine begins within a few minutes with a quick warm wave.","Warmth and euphoria rise fast.","The peak is strong and heroin-like but short.","The plateau lasts about an hour.","Effects fade within 2 to 3 hours.","Craving and irritability.","Tolerance and dependence build quickly; misuse spread in China in the 1990s."],
"ketobemidone":["Swallowed ketobemidone begins within about 15 to 30 minutes with warmth and lightness.","A quick, clean rise in mood with less itch than morphine.","The peak brings strong euphoria and pain relief; its NMDA-blocking action may make it useful for nerve pain.","A few hours of contentment.","Effects fade over 3 to 5 hours.","Constipation and sleepiness.","In Scandinavia it was known as one of the most addictive prescription opioids."],
"tilidine":["Tilidine drops or tablets begin within about 10 to 20 minutes, as the liver turns it into nortilidine, with warmth and a lift.","Users often report energy and talkativeness rather than sleepiness at first.","The peak is a bright, chatty euphoria with mild itch.","A plateau of 2 to 3 hours.","Effects fade over 3 to 5 hours.","Tiredness and irritability; the naloxone in Valoron N does nothing when swallowed but blocks effects if injected.","Low mood and craving with regular use; tilidine misuse has been a concern among young people in German cities."],
"oliceridine":["Given IV in hospitals, oliceridine starts working within about 2 to 5 minutes.","Drowsiness and pain relief rise quickly.","The peak brings moderate pain relief and sleepiness; nausea and vomiting are common.","Effects last around 1 to 3 hours.","They fade as the drug is cleared by the liver.","Nausea, dizziness.","Usually little next-day effect."],
"pholcodine":["Pholcodine syrup starts within about 30 minutes, quietening the cough reflex.","Mild drowsiness at most.","The peak is mostly cough relief; it has little pain relief or euphoria.","Cough relief lasts many hours because of a long half-life.","Fades over about 8 to 12 hours.","Mild drowsiness or constipation.","Little next-day effect."],
"nicocodeine":["Nicocodeine begins within about 20 to 40 minutes, a bit faster than codeine.","A warm, cough-quieting calm.","The peak is mild to moderate warmth and drowsiness.","A few hours.","Fades over 4 to 6 hours.","Constipation.","Little next-day effect."],
"acetyldihydrocodeine":["It begins within about 30 to 60 minutes with mild warmth.","Gentle drowsiness.","The peak is a mild codeine-like calm.","A few hours.","Fades over 4 to 6 hours.","Constipation.","Little next-day effect."],
"normethadone":["Normethadone starts slowly, about an hour after swallowing, with gentle warmth.","Slow calm.","The peak is a moderate, methadone-like heaviness.","Long plateau of several hours.","It fades over many hours.","Constipation and drowsiness.","Grogginess the next day."],
"bezitramide":["Bezitramide starts very slowly, 1 to 2 hours after swallowing, as it turns into its active form.","A creeping heaviness.","The peak is flat but long.","It stays active for many hours.","It fades over a day or more, which caused delayed, unexpected overdoses.","Constipation.","Still active the next day."],
"propiram":["Propiram starts within about 30 minutes with mild warmth.","Gentle drowsiness.","The peak is mild, limited by its partial action.","A few hours.","Fades over 3 to 5 hours.","Dizziness.","Little."],
"fentanyl-analogs":["Injected or smoked fentanyl analogs act within seconds; snorted within minutes.","A rush of heaviness with little warning.","The peak is strong and short, and strength varies hugely between analogs (some far weaker, some far stronger than fentanyl).","Under an hour to a few hours.","Effects fade fast, often within 2 to 4 hours, driving redosing.","Craving and early withdrawal.","Next-day withdrawal in regular users."],
"brorphine":["Brorphine, usually hidden in other drugs, acts within minutes when injected or smoked.","Sudden heaviness.","The peak is strong, fentanyl-like sedation.","A few hours.","Effects fade over several hours.","Exhaustion.","Withdrawal in regular users."],
"ap-237":["2-methyl-AP-237 begins within about 10 to 30 minutes when swallowed.","Warmth and mild euphoria.","The peak is moderate, shorter and lighter than morphine.","1 to 2 hours.","Fades over 2 to 4 hours, which drives repeated use.","Craving, low mood.","Withdrawal in daily users."],
"thebaine-oripavine":["Thebaine, if swallowed, acts within about 30 minutes, but not as a typical opioid.","Restlessness and unease rather than calm.","The peak can include muscle rigidity and convulsions.","Short.","Fades over a few hours.","Agitation.","Little."],
}
